  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p7, after eliminations); business-type = Nutrition Fund (p8-9). Loan proceeds 388,000 are in debt_proceeds, not receipts; printed total receipts 5,627,620 includes it (includes debt_proceeds). Governmental balances are fund balances (beginning 1,641,180, ending 1,591,512 = balance sheet total p5). The 25,000 General Fund transfer to the Activity Fund (General budget schedule p10 'Transfers'; Activity Fund 'Transfer from General Fund' p13) is eliminated in the total column of p7, so top-level transfers_in/out are null; in detail it is recorded as other financing (-25,000 in General, +25,000 in Activity). Transfer cross-check: Depreciation Fund budgeted 100,000 transfer in but actual 0; the p5/p4 due to/from 200,000 General/Building is an interfund balance, not a transfer. p6 General column Extracurricular 25,000 is the hidden transfer; the total column nets it out, so no contra needed. Detail: used budget schedules (General p10, Depreciation p11, Building p12) and combining statement of other governmental funds p13 (Student Fees Fund all zeros, skipped); zero-actual lines (Tuition, ESU receipts, Vehicle acquisition, Depreciation Fund transfers) omitted. General Fund detail by object is not provided; function totals recorded as not itemized. Building Fund and General Fund debt service lines split into principal/interest using the statements on p6-7. Statements of Accounts with County Treasurers (pp14-16, unaudited) are pass-through reconciliations and were not recorded as detail (they duplicate tax receipts already in the fund statements). Balance sheet uses the government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (p1), which excludes the component unit. Business-type measure recorded as cash (modified cash basis; net position = cash 84,804). Read pages 1-16 of 16"
}